  <doc-data|<doc-title|The four-dimensional Yang--Mills
  construction<next-line><with|font-size|1.19|Foundations and the existence
  argument>>|<doc-author|<author-data|<author-name|Humanise Yang--Mills
  contributors>>>|<doc-date|Working draft, 16 November 2026>>

  <no-indent><with|font-series|bold|Status.> This working draft presents the
  construction-bound existence theorem and its same-family proof. The final
  assembly identifies the quantitative producers, the all-period limits and
  the reconstruction in every character. The source correspondence and scoped
  independent agent reviews are recorded in the accompanying blueprint; they
  do not constitute independent human acceptance. The mathematical exposition
  remains a draft for review. No mass gap or uniqueness of the
  infinite-volume limit is claimed.

  <vspace*|1fn><no-indent><with|font-series|bold|Source and attribution.> The
  argument follows the Lean formalisation at
  <slink|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028>, pinned to
  revision

  <\padded-center>
    <with|font-family|tt|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  </padded-center>

  The initial source clustering and declaration maps used to organize this
  exposition come from Scott Armstrong's Yang\UMills informalization project,
  <slink|https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/yang-mills-informalization>.\ 

